 ## Descriptor ABI (binding map)
+
+Nested texture/sampler graphs that cannot use a fixed root/field coordinate carry
+`argument_resource_tables: {version: 2, table_binding: 672, categories: [...]}`.
+They require the default descriptor layout. Binding 672 in set 0 is the read-only token
+table; categories 0, 1, 2 denote runtime sampled-image, storage-image and sampler arrays
+at binding 0 of sets 2, 3, 4. The first six table words contain each category's
+`(word_offset, count)`, followed by sorted low/high token pairs. Descriptor index 0 is
+reserved for a dummy. Tokens are opaque identifiers, never GPU addresses. The shader
+loads them through its actual record/pointer graph, so this contract has no raw root
+descriptors. Consumers must bind these additional resources and enable the corresponding
+descriptor-indexing features. Unknown graph operations return an error. Flat resources
+with representable coordinates retain their existing static descriptor ABI.
 
 By default, every descriptor-backed Metal-facing resource uses **descriptor set 0**
 (`RESOURCE_DESCRIPTOR_SET`). Most default bindings are a fixed base plus Metal resource index `n`:
